<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Android auto-backup rules (API 30 and below; API 31+ uses data_extraction_rules.xml).

   The Navidrome password, the hub token and the AudioMuse token are in navic_secrets.xml,
   sealed with a key in this device's Android Keystore (B-279). The key is not backed up, so
   a restored copy could not be opened: the file is excluded, and a restored install asks for
   the password and the tokens again. The name is the same on debug and release builds (the
   file is named in code, not after the applicationId).

   The settings file stays excluded as before. It no longer holds a credential, but an install
   that has not opened since this change can still hold the old plaintext values until its
   first launch moves them. Multiplatform-Settings' `Settings()` maps to the default
   SharedPreferences file, <applicationId>_preferences.xml: "paige.navic", plus ".debug" on
   debug builds, so both are named.

   Cached library data lives in the Room databases and is re-syncable, so it is excluded too
   rather than dragging a stale copy of the library onto a new device.
-->
<full-backup-content>
	<exclude
		domain="sharedpref"
		path="navic_secrets.xml" />
	<exclude
		domain="sharedpref"
		path="paige.navic_preferences.xml" />
	<exclude
		domain="sharedpref"
		path="paige.navic.debug_preferences.xml" />
	<exclude
		domain="database"
		path="cache.db" />
	<exclude
		domain="database"
		path="downloads.db" />
</full-backup-content>
